Z||000002||StuGood||05-07-2001||10:17 PM||||Wait - !  My memory tells me that to bypass the clutch safety switch electrically, you <B>don't</B> want to short <B>anything</B> to ground!  If that's what you want to do, I believe you would want to connect the 2 terminals together, and <B>insulate</B> the connection.  <P>Now, I'm working from memory here - and I apologize if I'm wrong.  But be <B>sure</B> you know what you're doing before you short anything (especially the unfused starter circuitry) to ground!<P>I think JohnnyK is more interested in how to physically remove the safety switch from a clutch pedal.  And frankly I can't suggest anything better than what he says he's tried already  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ||||reg||4
